    "created_at": "2017-10-13T21:44:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-13T21:44:02Z",
    "body": "MutationObserver was explicitly designed to work that way, but I can't now recall the reasoning.\r\nI think it might have been something along the lines that for consistency every setAttribute call should create a record. Conceptually there is after all a mutation: there is an old value replaced with a new one, and whether or not they are the same doesn't really matter.\r\nAnd Custom elements should work the same way as MutationObserver.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
